\newlabel{fig:valsummary}{{8}{11}{Validation-sweep summary, \code {TP0014}--\code {TP0038} (firmware v3). Left: hold-window tracking error remains unbiased at every setpoint; the three inflated $\sigma $ bars are the residual failure runs. Center: hysteretic dropout-event count --- only 0.12, 0.15, and 0.87 cycle; the deep out-of-band endpoints 0 and 1 are clean latched cutoffs. Right: run-minimum bus voltage; only \code {TP0016} (0.15) collapses the bus}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {WP0040} (moving setpoint and load): measured share (orange) against the raw table setpoint (dashed) and the governed setpoint reconstructed from the firmware's clip law (mustard). The measured share follows the governed command everywhere the share is measurable; the flat 0.5 stretches at $t=25$--33\,s are the designed collapse below $2I_\mathrm  {min}$ of filtered total current, not tracking failure.}}{12}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:wp0040}{{9}{12}{\code {WP0040} (moving setpoint and load): measured share (orange) against the raw table setpoint (dashed) and the governed setpoint reconstructed from the firmware's clip law (mustard). The measured share follows the governed command everywhere the share is measurable; the flat 0.5 stretches at $t=25$--33\,s are the designed collapse below $2I_\mathrm {min}$ of filtered total current, not tracking failure}{figure.caption.14}{}}
