\newlabel{tab:v4faults}{{2}{18}{The six \code {ERR\_UV\_BUS} runs. ``Relay onset'' is the first exclusive-conduction handoff; ``first $<$12\,V'' is the first bus sample under the fault limit; ``latch delay'' is from that sample to the end of the log}{table.caption.22}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {TP0053} ($r^\ast =0.70$): the source-commutation relay cycle. Top: FC and BT alternate exclusive conduction with 2--3\,A reconnect bursts; co-conduction never occurs. Middle: each both-channels-off handoff window discharges the motor node, and the troughs walk monotonically down through the 12\,V fault limit as the load ramp steepens the discharge slope. Bottom: the commanded droop ratio sawtooths between reproducible commutation thresholds at the slew-limited rate.}}{19}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tp0053relay}{{14}{19}{\code {TP0053} ($r^\ast =0.70$): the source-commutation relay cycle. Top: FC and BT alternate exclusive conduction with 2--3\,A reconnect bursts; co-conduction never occurs. Middle: each both-channels-off handoff window discharges the motor node, and the troughs walk monotonically down through the 12\,V fault limit as the load ramp steepens the discharge slope. Bottom: the commanded droop ratio sawtooths between reproducible commutation thresholds at the slew-limited rate}{figure.caption.23}{}}
